{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RYAPD3dZytCBxcARAZRQYQ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d7c6630e6bc2b84be38b0e9881ae77feaae1de70159a140087c40981d7a3d2b7\",\"sha256\":\"d7c6630e6bc2b84be38b0e9881ae77feaae1de70159a140087c40981d7a3d2b7\"},\"id\":\"claude-review-expectation-task\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=1cfeafee74b6ce601b793d148adb87d5cb11243577e60fbf5fdbef67ae025eeb]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Actual claude Reviewer: expectation\\n\\nRoot selects the frozen claim in SELECTION.json. Read-only assessment; no source/candidate edits, repair, package installation, Git, model/subagent call or acceptance. Public a_c CLI writes only its own protected evidence. Bash/Read may inspect permitted sources and perform bounded in-memory/read-only probes. Do not write request files: use call --request - with an in-memory JSON envelope.\\n\\nAcquire the governing sources through review.prepare phase=expectation, expectation_body=null, proof=[] and the exact claim/candidate coordinates. Do not acquire any candidate population bytes. Read the operation evidence to obtain its actual acquisitions ArtifactRefs. Derive your own falsifiable expectations, then call review.prepare phase=expectation with expectation_body={text: your actual wording, source_inputs: those prior acquisition refs}; expectations=null. Return the actual expectation ArtifactRef, source-first/exposure facts and limitations. No candidate assessment is performed. This partial return cannot be consumed as final review because its frozen proof.expectations is null.\\n\\nThe governing source route is SELECTION.governing_sources. Candidate coordinates are metadata, not permission to read them before expectations. Shared requirements may govern tenant assessment, but common-WHAT candidate clauses cannot simultaneously be a pre-exposure governing source for their own review. If the selection has that overlap, return the exact missing basis instead of inventing source-first standing. Prior review expectations/verdicts are not your oracle. Disclose bootstrap/external exposure; no fresh context or family label certifies independence.\\n\\nUse the exact current native profile and tools.describe where needed. Native results.conjoin is unsupported. Source ownership and source-first law are the selected STDO3.0.1 release; no methodology duplication or stronger universal ceremony. Report S0-S4 findings with file:line, exact violated relation, reachable evidence and consequence; separate evidence from causal/repair inference. Record unperformed host qualification and efficiency claims as open, not pass/fail totals.\\n\\nThe public review.prepare request envelope is {\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"unique-id\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"review.prepare\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"phase\\\":\\\"expectation\\\" or \\\"candidate\\\",\\\"claim\\\":the CLAIM SourceRef,\\\"sources\\\":SELECTION.governing_sources,\\\"candidate\\\":SELECTION.candidate,\\\"proof\\\":[] for expectation or the selected proof SourceRefs,\\\"comparison\\\":null,\\\"expectations\\\":null for expectation or the bound ArtifactRef for candidate,\\\"expectation_body\\\":null for acquisition, then {\\\"text\\\":your actual source-derived expectations,\\\"source_inputs\\\":[actual prior acquisition ArtifactRefs]} when recording expectations}}. Source reads use arguments {\\\"source\\\":SourceRef,\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}. Evidence reads use {\\\"artifact\\\":ArtifactRef}. The first review.prepare response's evidence points to an OperationEvidence; evidence.read reveals envelope.payload.acquisitions, the actual source_inputs. Do not use OperationEvidence references where Acquisition references are required. Acquisition alone is not expectation recording: make the second expectation call with your own text.\\n\\nClosed return has exactly schema, id, frame, activation, subject, basis, actor, consumer, evaluations, not_performed, work_result, residuals, invalidators. schema=\\\"a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1\\\"; frame={id,revision}, activation={id,sha256}, subject={id,sha256}, basis={method_profile:{id,sha256},observations:[ArtifactRef]}, actor={id,family,authorship}, copied from actual Context. Each evaluation has exactly id, predicate (exact PREDICATES SourceRef), domain_outcome, core_value, evidence, residuals, invalidators. evidence contains actual SourceRefs/ArtifactRefs; residuals/invalidators are arrays. work_result=null. Use the return contract's evaluation id. A source-first expectation phase returns expectation-recording only, with the expectation artifact in evidence/domain_outcome; it does not assess the candidate.\\n\\nThis phase has 300 seconds within a 1200-second aggregate Reviewer budget; no retry. Inherited configured model/effort defaults remain unchanged. Final output is one original closed-return JSON object, no fences. Perform only the return contract's named evaluation and cite actual evidence; put unperformed evaluation IDs in not_performed. Candidate phase findings and per-component conclusions belong in domain_outcome. Never repair or replace the final original. Root owns continuation.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"d8db4d98851bd2ab5be84e41fda5321045aa4a450ccd8859b8b3fc696af1971f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"d8db4d98851bd2ab5be84e41fda5321045aa4a450ccd8859b8b3fc696af1971f\",\"size_bytes\":4561,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"claude-setup2/expectation/TASK.md\",\"root\":\"review\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"d8db4d98851bd2ab5be84e41fda5321045aa4a450ccd8859b8b3fc696af1971f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38","uuid":"6d6b5178-cdef-4696-b4ec-90295f2ee8e0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:30:59.251Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d7c6630e6bc2b84be38b0e9881ae77feaae1de70159a140087c40981d7a3d2b7\",\"sha256\":\"d7c6630e6bc2b84be38b0e9881ae77feaae1de70159a140087c40981d7a3d2b7\"},\"id\":\"claude-review-expectation-task\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=1cfeafee74b6ce601b793d148adb87d5cb11243577e60fbf5fdbef67ae025eeb]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Actual claude Reviewer: expectation\\n\\nRoot selects the frozen claim in SELECTION.json. Read-only assessment; no source/candidate edits, repair, package installation, Git, model/subagent call or acceptance. Public a_c CLI writes only its own protected evidence. Bash/Read may inspect permitted sources and perform bounded in-memory/read-only probes. Do not write request files: use call --request - with an in-memory JSON envelope.\\n\\nAcquire the governing sources through review.prepare phase=expectation, expectation_body=null, proof=[] and the exact claim/candidate coordinates. Do not acquire any candidate population bytes. Read the operation evidence to obtain its actual acquisitions ArtifactRefs. Derive your own falsifiable expectations, then call review.prepare phase=expectation with expectation_body={text: your actual wording, source_inputs: those prior acquisition refs}; expectations=null. Return the actual expectation ArtifactRef, source-first/exposure facts and limitations. No candidate assessment is performed. This partial return cannot be consumed as final review because its frozen proof.expectations is null.\\n\\nThe governing source route is SELECTION.governing_sources. Candidate coordinates are metadata, not permission to read them before expectations. Shared requirements may govern tenant assessment, but common-WHAT candidate clauses cannot simultaneously be a pre-exposure governing source for their own review. If the selection has that overlap, return the exact missing basis instead of inventing source-first standing. Prior review expectations/verdicts are not your oracle. Disclose bootstrap/external exposure; no fresh context or family label certifies independence.\\n\\nUse the exact current native profile and tools.describe where needed. Native results.conjoin is unsupported. Source ownership and source-first law are the selected STDO3.0.1 release; no methodology duplication or stronger universal ceremony. Report S0-S4 findings with file:line, exact violated relation, reachable evidence and consequence; separate evidence from causal/repair inference. Record unperformed host qualification and efficiency claims as open, not pass/fail totals.\\n\\nThe public review.prepare request envelope is {\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"unique-id\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"review.prepare\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"phase\\\":\\\"expectation\\\" or \\\"candidate\\\",\\\"claim\\\":the CLAIM SourceRef,\\\"sources\\\":SELECTION.governing_sources,\\\"candidate\\\":SELECTION.candidate,\\\"proof\\\":[] for expectation or the selected proof SourceRefs,\\\"comparison\\\":null,\\\"expectations\\\":null for expectation or the bound ArtifactRef for candidate,\\\"expectation_body\\\":null for acquisition, then {\\\"text\\\":your actual source-derived expectations,\\\"source_inputs\\\":[actual prior acquisition ArtifactRefs]} when recording expectations}}. Source reads use arguments {\\\"source\\\":SourceRef,\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}. Evidence reads use {\\\"artifact\\\":ArtifactRef}. The first review.prepare response's evidence points to an OperationEvidence; evidence.read reveals envelope.payload.acquisitions, the actual source_inputs. Do not use OperationEvidence references where Acquisition references are required. Acquisition alone is not expectation recording: make the second expectation call with your own text.\\n\\nClosed return has exactly schema, id, frame, activation, subject, basis, actor, consumer, evaluations, not_performed, work_result, residuals, invalidators. schema=\\\"a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1\\\"; frame={id,revision}, activation={id,sha256}, subject={id,sha256}, basis={method_profile:{id,sha256},observations:[ArtifactRef]}, actor={id,family,authorship}, copied from actual Context. Each evaluation has exactly id, predicate (exact PREDICATES SourceRef), domain_outcome, core_value, evidence, residuals, invalidators. evidence contains actual SourceRefs/ArtifactRefs; residuals/invalidators are arrays. work_result=null. Use the return contract's evaluation id. A source-first expectation phase returns expectation-recording only, with the expectation artifact in evidence/domain_outcome; it does not assess the candidate.\\n\\nThis phase has 300 seconds within a 1200-second aggregate Reviewer budget; no retry. Inherited configured model/effort defaults remain unchanged. Final output is one original closed-return JSON object, no fences. Perform only the return contract's named evaluation and cite actual evidence; put unperformed evaluation IDs in not_performed. Candidate phase findings and per-component conclusions belong in domain_outcome. Never repair or replace the final original. Root owns continuation.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"d8db4d98851bd2ab5be84e41fda5321045aa4a450ccd8859b8b3fc696af1971f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"d8db4d98851bd2ab5be84e41fda5321045aa4a450ccd8859b8b3fc696af1971f\",\"size_bytes\":4561,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"claude-setup2/expectation/TASK.md\",\"root\":\"review\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"d8db4d98851bd2ab5be84e41fda5321045aa4a450ccd8859b8b3fc696af1971f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RYAPD3dZytCBxcARAZRQYQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
