ecovery.md\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"d7f7f118eea492bb64456a56c4cb4987e6e23acd8b3c0143ba87cf5ec9a92c80\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/release-install.md\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"ec7cb5a407f6690936d0bf79ab5fc8796c2cfca4c34772f61ceff4b68f337cfb\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"8bb49c0dfe0eb87fbfbe5063c4a43e15f074e25fdd4ff90ffdec24ef14e75c8b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/source-routes.json\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"09972e4af512645c43207aa3edd5114e1e81c24ef344c76a6af2e99852920403\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"build_tenants/codex/tests/verify_package.py\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"65ec9851967a60ab6f25f4c988b2ddbc05642ce44ae71401d6f1bf99f5ec0086\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:claude:cross-family-review:1\"\n}\n\n\n################ SOURCE review USER-OUTCOME.md None sel_sha 008f733c9a6ee68e973ddebbaf71b8cb4106fd3f6b9af61a7e44c6d1c4579235 acq {}\n# Original user outcome selected for this review\n\nThe user's actual instructions in this session included:\n\n> the tools have not been maintained and i'd apply stdo design principles itself the tools need to harmonise with stdo 3.0.1\n\n> we are going to create two build tenants for skills codex & claude\n\n> the requirements are the same but the build tenants are different especially as each may need tuning to its type\n\n> yes the are decoupled, this is a test, eating our own dog food,\n> 1. pin stdo 3.0.1 as the static released methodology against specification_method\n> 2. as executive build out of stdo skills, use the current tooling to build the skills\n\nRoot selected a separate root-level stdo_skills Product, with shared WHAT and independent host-specific HOW tenants, under the verified immutable released STDO3.0.1 basis. This statement records the user's outcome and Root's scope selection; it does not import the candidate's wording as its own oracle. No RC formalisation, remote publication, general benefit, reliability or complete methodological qualification is claimed.\n\n\n################ SOURCE method standards/EVALUATION.md {'lines': [177, 248]} sel_sha d5e8cd4f574cebc1728e1aefafd5cd05763ab782f872bce3f29d7c8649e442c9 acq {}\n## 3. Independent assessment\n\nA constructor's self-review is construction output, not assessment. Where\npromotion needs independent assessment, the assessor evaluates the exact\nlive subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not the\nconstructor's summary (P6, and P0 with its premise that a step's output is\na candidate until evaluated; instance premise (c) of §1 Foundation to law).\nThis section decides what counts as independent assessment. Which\nboundaries require it is a policy choice of the Spec Method, owned by\n[TICKETS §7 Execution and verification authority separation](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007);\na governing basis may add boundaries.\n\nProtocol: where method qualification applies\n([§7 Method self-qualification](#method-self-qualification)), the subject is\nfrozen by identity before material reference exposure; elsewhere it is\nstabilised by an immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation\nsufficient for the claimed assessment. The assessor records its\nexpectations from the governing source before opening the candidate; it\nreads the subject at that identity or relation, never a mutable working\ntree; it makes no repair; it does not assess its\nown authorship. Reusing the constructor's judgment does not satisfy\nindependence; shared mechanical evidence may be reused, judgment may not\n(ACTIVATION §7). Binding a returned assessment to its producer, subject,\nbasis and evidence authenticates the result; it establishes neither the\nassertion provenance of its expected answer nor the execution provenance\nof its run, which\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Parallel derivation and mutual assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance)\nrequires separately (P6, P3). Membership in a plan authenticates nothing,\nan unauthenticated result satisfies no required assessment, and a result\nbound to another subject satisfies no planned assessment\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results));\nno cryptographic or transport protocol is prescribed for the binding (P6). Any post-exposure revision is a declared intervention: it\nis either a method constituent with its own qualification boundary or a new\nqualification subject, and it cannot retroactively make the original\nfrozen construction pass. This law prescribes no actor type or count,\nreview-round count, engine, prompt or orchestration (P6).\n\nAuthor identity is the party responsible for the content of a realised\nsubject. It is distinct from actor identity, whoever performs one\noperation, which is an identity and not an authority\n([FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)).\nAuthorship is one of the conditions on\nwhich the independence of an assessment rests; the evidence conditions are\nthe other (P6, P3).\n\nReporting a defect, supplying a counterexample or identifying behaviour\nalready required by governing law does not by itself author the realised\nsubject. Contributing wording, design or policy that is adopted into the\nsubject, including through directions for a particular repair, is authorship\nof that contribution. A\nreporter may assess a later repair only when the existing assessment grant,\nauthorship relation and evidence-independence conditions permit it; a\nreporter gains no review authority from having found the defect. A person\nwho authored an adopted repair cannot supply its required independent\nassessment by calling that authorship a finding (P6, P3).\n\nIndependence rests on authorship and on the evidence conditions above, not\non a new context. The assessor may read the same governing sources as the\nconstructor. A fresh context alone establishes no independence, and it\nsupplies no review authority the author lacks: an author that opens a\nfresh context to review its own candidate is still its author, and its\nreview is self-review, which stays construction output and cannot be\nrelabelled as independent assessment (P6;\n[TICKETS UP-007](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007)). A contribution received from another author stays that\nauthor's wherever it is carried, and that author's reading of it supplies\nno independent acceptance of it (P6).\n\nIndependence across actor families is declared, not assumed. Whether two\nactivations of one model family are independent for a semantic judgment is a\npolicy the governing basis states for the claim; the default where it is not\nstated is that they are not independent.\n\n\n\n################ SOURCE method standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md {'lines': [957, 1009]} sel_sha fc549bf2e55ffaabad86b4fd3b9290d9043f8716f2ed21b28c0410c643c3911c acq {}\n## 10. Derived Reviewer frame\n\n(P6, P5)\n\n| Frame element | Reviewer |\n|---|---|\n| evaluation family | Is this the exact claimed subject and basis? Does it satisfy the applicable method and project relations without competing authority, proof masking or an unevaluated composition boundary? For each finding, which evidence-bound severity and technical implications follow? |\n| subject and basis | exact candidate, claim, governing method and project authority, scope, exclusions, evidence population, Product-selected severity scale, review carrier and declared independence conditions |\n| material manifold | claimed relations; causal producers and consumers; authority seams; competing paths; failure, recovery, installed and reconstruction surfaces where claimed; test and fixture semantics; historical counterexamples; a finding's cause, blast radius, workaround, repair complexity, regression risk and uncertainty where supportable |\n| coordinates | exact candidate, source basis, authority revision, configuration, dependency, evidence population, severity scale, installed subject, review time and Reviewer identity |\n| governing invariants | RF-001 to RF-017; the execution relation (ACTIVATION §1 and §3); independence and traceability (EVALUATION §3); assurance boundary and qualification freeze (EVALUATION §1, §3 and §7); applicable Product, design, identity and release law |\n| authority | bounded evaluation only; review access yields no construction, transformation, admission, publication, mutation, decision, disposition or next-activation authority |\n| evidence | independently acquired live authority, candidate implementation, tests, artifacts, history, operational evidence, mutations, replay or reconstruction, and reproduced observations material to the claim and the technical triage |\n| capability envelope | declared method, domain, implementation, assurance, technical-triage, tool, access, context, counterexample-search and independence competence |\n| exclusions | editing the candidate, implementing a repair, assigning priority, disposing the release or MVP boundary, selecting the next action, substituting the Worker's summary, assurance-owned semantic reconstruction, flattening unbound evidence, silent scope expansion |\n| result | one core result with findings, counterexamples, evidence-bound technical triage and residuals sufficient for the Executive to assign priority and apply the existing disposition where the basis is decidable |\n| invalidation | a material change of candidate, authority, basis, evidence population, severity scale, dependency, configuration, scope or independence |\n\nWhen independent review is required, and what makes a claimed review\ntraceable, are\n[TICKETS UP-007](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007),\nwith the further boundaries a governing basis adds; what counts as\nindependent is [EVALUATION §3](EVALUATION.md#3-independent-assessment);\nEVALUATION §1, §3 and §7 decide the exact assurance boundary and the\nqualification freeze. This profile adds no universal review round and no\nnew independence test (P6).\n\nACTIVATION §1 and §3 stay the owners of assessment and disposition. This\nprofile uses an activated Reviewer result as independent live-surface\nevaluation input and, in the coordinated branch, the Executive as the\nauthorised assessor or proxy that applies the one existing disposition. It\ncreates no second verdict or disposition family (P6, P5).\n\nThe Reviewer may assess likely repair complexity and regression risk\nwithout becoming the repair owner. Where cause, blast radius, workaround or\nrepair risk cannot be supported inside the activation, the result records\nthat uncertainty instead of manufacturing a complete triage (P5).\n\nTests are inside the Reviewer's manifold when their code, fixtures,\nmutations, environment or interpretation can change the proof claim; a\npassing result is not relied on in place of reviewing those semantics (P6,\nEVALUATION §1).\n\nEach finding binds a violated property, a supported entry or state, the\ngoverning operating or threat model and a credible causal path. The same\nconditions apply to retained guards and acceptance predicates as to new\nfindings. An excluded threat alone gives no retention claim; a proposed\nwider threat model re-enters its owner. Internal location alone does not\nestablish trust, and hypothetical hostility alone does not establish\napplicability. The actual untrusted-input, mutable-state, authority and\neffect checks the supported model requires are retained. A suggested repair\nbecomes an obligation only through its proper owner (P6, P2, P5).\n\n\n\n################ SOURCE method standards/ACTIVATION.md {'lines': [1004, 1055]} sel_sha 503cf7de07bd21bd57279b2e6bae3b29db70ad3cc24a169474656475c39cefd8 acq {}\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\nexists (P5, P6):\n\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\n|---|---|---|\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\n\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\n\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\n\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \"a candidate is available\", never\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\n(P5, P6).\n\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\n(P6).\n\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\nP3).\n\n### Disposition\n\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\nsemantic dispositions (§1, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\n([EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\n\n\n################ SOURCE method standards/ACTIVATION.md {'lines': [1750, 1768]} sel_sha 08d23dd3949b21b80e23fa46bffedff55bfa456a51e1afd8df831b5f13bbd216 acq {}\n### Transition evidence\n\nA reviewable transition identifies the exact candidate, the affected\nrelations, the changed realisation paths, the authority paths added or\nremoved, the retained and open seams, the focused proof, any required\nintegration proof, the explicit non-changes, and, where an assessor was\nactivated, the assessor's recommended disposition, with the decision\nowner's disposition beside it once one is made (§3). Consumers\nchoose the representation. Transition evidence is a read\nmodel; it does not become specification, design or admission authority\n(P6, P4b).\n\nConstruction uses the cheapest focused proof capable of falsifying the\nactive relation. Expensive whole-candidate qualification occurs at a\ndeclared candidate boundary rather than after every local edit, unless the\naffected risk makes whole-candidate proof necessary (§6). A durable or\nreconstructable authority claim is not established solely by a same-process\nproof when loss of incidental process state is a material counterexample:\nthe proof destroys or excludes the incidental authority and compares the\n\n\n################ SOURCE method standards/SPEC_METHOD.md {'lines': [1755, 1835]} sel_sha d1c84116532b06404eb6470672e1261a2daf2cf83798a561e91f56eb21ad7a5b acq {}\n## 11. Build-tenant binding\n\nThis section owns the relation between a product's WHAT and the build\ntenants that realise it: what a tenant binds, what stays fixed while it\nchooses, and what its evidence shows. It applies to every product built\nwith this method (P2, P1, P6).\n\nTerms used in this section:\n\n- A build tenant is one independent, project-owned HOW realisation of a\n  product's WHAT. The build-tenancy context of\n  [PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#8-what-how-and-work-carriers)\n  names it, and the product definition's tenant registry locates each one.\n- The requirements calculus of a product is the set of obligations its\n  WHAT states, the outcomes it permits, and its rules for refining and\n  composing the work that realises it.\n- A computational calculus is a declared set of executable operations,\n  with the laws by which they compose, the transformations they permit,\n  and their effects and resource behaviour, as far as these are material\n  to the obligations.\n- An execution environment is the concrete means that performs those\n  operations: a technology stack; a human process, made of people, roles,\n  documents, communication channels and decision procedures; or a\n  combination of the two.\n- A tenant's build-tenant binding has two parts: its calculus binding,\n  from the requirements calculus to its computational calculus, and its\n  execution binding, from that computational calculus to its execution\n  environment. A tenant's registry entry locates the tenant; it is not the\n  binding.\n- A generic procedure is a method procedure whose scope is independent of\n  the selected execution environment. It and its projections preserve the\n  bindings Rule 2 permits: code, an event stream or reconstruction from a\n  complete history is required only where the governing obligations or\n  the selected execution binding require it, and an adequate human\n  process using current records and direct observation is a permitted\n  execution binding of a generic procedure that requires none of them\n  (P1, P6).\n- Author identity and actor identity are as\n  [EVALUATION §3](EVALUATION.md#3-independent-assessment) defines them:\n  authorship is one condition of an assessment's independence there, and\n  an actor's identity is not an authority.\n  Operation kind is what an operation does, such as construct, assess,\n  relay, record, measure or decide, together with the authority that kind\n  of operation requires.\n\nThe common deterministic functor kind is a separate coordinate owned by\n[AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §5](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#5-traversals-and-functor-kinds).\nA binding that claims F_D establishes the common kind's total-domain contract.\nIt retains the operation's subject, evidence and effect permissions. Human,\nmachine and mixed bindings preserve these same distinctions; no runtime,\nevent log or annotation carrier follows from the classification.\n\nRules:\n\n1. Realisations of one WHAT. One WHAT is realised by one or more\n   independent build tenants, whatever the physical layout. The WHAT is\n   constitutional and each tenant's realisation is HOW; a tenant-local\n   realisation stays derivative until its governing truth is ratified in\n   specification (§2). Each tenant binds the product's requirements\n   calculus to a declared computational calculus and binds that calculus\n   to a concrete execution environment. Both bindings are that tenant's\n   design and realisation: they are declared in its existing design and\n   realisation surfaces, chosen under the Design rule (§2) and recorded as\n   design decisions (§10), and the method requires no further carrier. The\n   tenant owns its binding, its realisation and their evidence; the WHAT\n   keeps its meaning (P2, P6).\n2. Selection. The execution environment may be a technology stack, a\n   human process or a combination. Its selection stays within the\n   requirements calculus, including every human decision that calculus\n   requires: no choice of environment removes a required human decision or\n   a required independent assessment. Author identity, actor identity and\n   operation kind stay distinct, and none determines another. Who authored\n   a tenant does not select its environment; one actor may perform\n   operations of several kinds, each under its own grant; and an actor's\n   identity neither decides the kind of an operation nor grants authority\n   for it. A person performing an operation does not by that make it human\n   adjudication: §5 states the admission that makes an operation human\n   adjudication and how a person who decides under policy without it is\n   governed. The same holds for every decision the requirements reserve to\n   a human: the person the governing authority admits for it takes it, and\n   a person's part elsewhere in the process does not (P6, P1).\n\n\n################ SOURCE method standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md {'lines': [919, 1062]} sel_sha 25b0cece8f1fd058d6645b94a9305c3c926b7c56a6d5315c290674750dbbbf48 acq {}\n## 5. Traversals and functor kinds\n\nA traversal is a typed contract (P4a, P6):\n\n```text\nv = {\n  id,\n  domain,\n  codomain,\n  context,\n  owner,\n  scope,\n  basis,\n  preconditions,\n  postconditions,\n  authority,\n  evidence,\n  provenance,\n  stop_states\n}\n```\n\nThe traversal record is this member's own concept. A same-spelled term\nowned by a profile, a realisation or a runtime is not imported by nominal\nequality and does not specialise this record except through a declared\nbinding under that owner's authority (§9; P3, P1).\n\n`a_c` defines three fundamental functor-kind identities (P3):\n\n```text\nF_D = urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-d\nF_P = urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-p\nF_H = urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-h\n```\n\nApplication notation is:\n\n```text\nF_K[v](X_v) -> Y_v | Omega_v\n```\n\nwhere `F_K` is one functor kind, `v` is one exact traversal identity,\n`X_v` and `Y_v` are its typed input and result domains, and `Omega_v` is\nits closed stop algebra. `Omega_v` is a refinement of the core result\nalgebra of [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results): it adds no\ncore value, and each of its stop values maps to exactly one core value,\nnever to `satisfied`. A stop this member writes, `hold`, `gap`,\n`refusal(constraint)` or `refusal(basis)`, has the meaning and the core\nvalue that AC-007 gives it. The signature's stop contract declares any\nfurther stop value with the one core value it maps to, and may refine a\nstop value by cause. A traversal record's `stop_states` binds the stop\nmapping of that traversal, exactly one core value for each stop value; it\nmay refine a value of the signature's stop contract further by cause for\nthat traversal. Each refined value, whether the stop contract or a\n`stop_states` declares it, names its parent value and its cause and maps\nto its parent's core value: a value refined from `hold` to indeterminate,\nfrom `gap` or `refusal(basis)` to invalid_basis, and from\n`refusal(constraint)` to falsified. No refined value takes `satisfied`. A\ndifferent core value needs a different parent value, which only the member\nthat owns the parent declares; for these four stops that member is this\none. Neither the stop contract nor a traversal's `stop_states` raises a\nresult's standing (P5, P6). Purpose and material relation: one stop of one\ntraversal has one core value, so its consumers cannot read it two ways,\nand no refinement gives a stop another core value, so a violated\nconstraint never becomes a case that the evidence merely cannot decide.\n\n- `F_D` classifies total deterministic processing under an exact traversal\n  contract. An application declares `f_B:D_B->Outcome_B`, its closed logical\n  domain, exact basis, all material computational state and dependencies,\n  and its termination argument. For every domain input it terminates with\n  exactly one declared outcome. Closed domains may be infinite when\n  termination and outcome determination are established. Open-world\n  semantic choice and undeclared clock, filesystem or global dependencies\n  are outside this contract (P3, P4a, P6).\n\n  Here B is the exact basis of v, D_B is its declared logical input domain\n  X_v (including material state and resource inputs), and Outcome_B is the\n  declared result-or-stop domain Y_v | Omega_v. The function f_B determines\n  one such outcome, including a stop with its closed report where declared;\n  that report and its stop are not two outcomes. An enclosing step's output\n  availability remains a separate predicate.\n\n  State-dependent processing declares input state and the meaning of its\n  returned next state and value. Refusal and exhaustion retain their cause\n  and evaluated predicate. The signature and traversal bind each stop to\n  exactly one core value, never satisfied; an exhausted tag alone supplies\n  no mapping. Construction availability and assessment retain their\n  separate predicates and results, and an unperformed assessment has no\n  result. A fuel-bounded operation is distinct from the potentially\n  divergent operation it bounds. A deterministic decision or effect proposal\n  establishes no physical completion, runtime admission, permission or\n  quality (P5, P6; [ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition)).\n- `F_P` classifies bounded probabilistic interpretation, construction or\n  proposal under an exact traversal contract. Its result has no semantic,\n  admission, acceptance or closure authority merely because it is useful\n  or repeatable (P6, P0; instance premise (iii) of §1 Foundation to law).\n- `F_H` classifies explicit human adjudication under an exact identity,\n  authority grant, subject, basis and decision contract. Human presence\n  grants no ambient authority (P6).\n\nThe actor, the executor, the domain operation and the functor kind are\ndifferent coordinates. `Encode`, `Interpret`, `Serialize`, `Measure` and\nother named domain operations are not aliases for `F_D`, `F_P` or `F_H`.\nDifferent traversals may share one functor kind without sharing identity,\nsemantics, inputs, outputs, authority or evidence (P3, P6).\n\nClassifying an operation as F_D grants no semantic, evaluation, operation\nor decision authority. This is the kind-specific application of\n[AC-005](#ac-005-authority-conservation) and\n[FOUNDATIONS Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds): the exact\noperation contract and admitted grant determine its permissions and\nconsequences. Consumers apply this boundary to their own operations.\n\nEvaluation-operation profile. An operation declared to evaluate an unchanged\nsubject identifies that subject, admissible reads, witness or log outputs,\npermitted writes, stops and results, authority and invalidation conditions.\nIt preserves the judged subject and does not perform the domain construction\nit judges. Separately authorized persistence of a witness does not perform\nthe judged domain construction. A construction or mutation needs its own\noperation contract and grant; reporting a changed subject's property as the\noriginal subject's property violates this evaluation contract (P6, P3).\n\nClosedness concerns dependencies material to the computation, not complete\nworld knowledge. This kind's totality is stronger than total handling of\nconditions in [ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#4-totality-and-refinement).\nUnbounded work is not automatically `F_P` when a totality argument is missing.\nThe calculus does not classify every executable process as one of its kinds.\nA new non-total deterministic process is outside qualifying F_D. A route to\nan F_D claim is a separately identified bounded successor with its own\ndomain, outcomes, dependency closure and termination argument; a fuel bound\nis one possible construction. This proves nothing about the unbounded\noriginal. Other work remains governed by its selected operation and execution\nbasis without being asserted to be a qualifying a_c application.\nExisting operations enter this edition only through the evidence-sensitive\n[migration relation](RELEASE.md#deterministic-kind-migration). The\n[finite examples](examples/DETERMINISTIC_CONTRACTS.md) distinguish construction,\nassessment, proposed effects and three predicate-specific exhaustion cases.\n\n\"Functor kind\" is an `a_c` term for this traversal classification. It does\nnot by itself assert a category-theoretic functor. A model that claims\ncategorical functor laws carries the demonstration that\n[FOUNDATIONS §4](FOUNDATIONS.md#4-algebra), Formal fragment, requires of\nevery categorical claim (P6, P1).\n\n\n\n################ SOURCE tool specification/PRODUCT.md {'lines': [46, 135]} sel_sha ac2d263037328fa38d359119989e287404afd2988bc8f2231e7aa3f22bcdcbea acq {}\n## F_D support for F_P development actors\n\nThe Product additionally provides deterministic support tools for F_P\nExecutives, Workers and Reviewers building in a Specification Methodology\nworkspace. STDO3.0 owns the methodology and consequently the contracts these\ntools support: lifecycle, role duties, triage/re-entry, frame/activation,\napplicability, admission, results/conjunction, review/independence and acceptance.\nThe tools consume those contracts through an exact caller-selected method/profile\nbinding. a_c owns their supplied inputs, outputs, checked properties, public use\nand qualification; it does not create a second lifecycle or coordinate F_P work.\n\n| Deterministic support | Use by F_P actors |\n|---|---|\n| Discover tool contracts; bind/observe exact Product, method and current workspace | Executive, Worker and Reviewer identify supported operations, input identities, current material bytes and explicit unsupported contracts. |\n| Resolve records/raw source/grounding; query authored dependencies, impact and coverage | All three acquire deciding content and declared relationships. Executive uses them for its selections; Workers inspect the affected implementation/proof; Reviewers acquire source and evidence independently. |\n| Assemble/check caller-selected reference-frame context; preflight execution contracts | Render the method-owned activation from supplied selections and exact content; check the declared closure, envelope, bindings and Product-bound admission evidence without inventing authority. |\n| Dispatch through a selected executor; retain observations and notifications | Supply exact context/settings and the existing grant, and expose acknowledgment, output, observed effects, partial evidence and exceptions to the declared consumer. |\n| Capture/check closed returns; prepare review comparisons; execute declared checks and joins | Preserve actor outputs and their provenance; inspect exact candidate/source/proof, detect binding errors, and evaluate only supported supplied predicates or method-owned operators. |\n| Project/record existing work and evidence; prepare affected refresh/handoff; retain usage | Read existing owned carriers and apply already-authorized records through named Writer interfaces; preserve actual support, unresolved impact/effects and measured attempt costs across sessions. |\n\nThese are tools available at the points where the selected method and F_P actor\nneed them, not an a_c stage sequence, task-state store or agent topology.\nPublic interfaces must support direct Worker and Reviewer source/context/proof\naccess as well as Executive use. Commands, MCP/protocols, storage, executor,\nprovider and concrete schemas remain tenant HOW. Existing work/evidence owners\nremain authoritative; a tool view or recorded recommendation is not a decision.\n\nIn the target calculus, `F_D[v]` is deterministic evaluation/proof over declared\nproperties and returns a judgment. Source acquisition, context rendering,\nserialization, dispatch and authorized recording are named domain operations\nwith their own contracts; the `F_D` label does not merge their identities or\nconfer effects. The deterministic wrapper may invoke an F_P actor, but its\nsemantic output remains F_P. Qualified deterministic evaluation of an already-\ndeclared predicate or method-owned conjunction is supported only within its\nexplicit checked fragment; F_P supplies semantic selection and unresolved\njudgment. Existing source-to-model F_P authoring remains a separate capability,\nnot one of these new deterministic evaluations.\n\n## Method ownership and basis roles\n\nThe [source-owner map](requirements/fd-source-owner-map.md) binds provisional\nSTDO3.0 derivation reference commit\n`494451522072ec34381c644f1ccfa2331f2b1e27`, package\n`specification_methodology/v3/build_tenants/common/`, tree\n`082df4ea2b7b3658aab528bbfbcfe81234ccc810`, with exact member digests and deciding\nclauses for each tool requirement. That common candidate is not accepted,\nreleased or installed. It identifies the contracts from which the requested\ntoolset is derived; it is not an operative a_c constitution or a published v3\nrelease identity.\n\nThis implementation's builder remains the exact installed STDO v2.5.1-rc.2\nselected in `stdo_a_c.json`. A consumer workspace's exact selected operative\nmethod/profile is a separate input, and represented subject versions are another\nbasis role. A supported binding or explicitly qualified translation must resolve\nthose inputs; label equality, file presence and co-location do not compose them.\nNo implicit latest adoption, V3 runtime dependency, sibling Product composition,\nmethod acceptance or frozen-model regeneration follows from this source work.\n\n## Delivery and qualification boundary\n\nThe [deterministic support requirements](requirements/fd-support-tools.md) and\n[qualification scenarios](requirements/fd-support-verification.md) specify the\nrequested Product outcome. Their earlier Deferred/design-pending statements\ndescribe the T-007 specification-only cut. Under\n[T-008](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-008-fd-tenant-implementation.md#current-provisional-implementation),\nthe Graphify tenant has an operative selected HOW and provisional public\nimplementation; bounded implementation, independent code review and technical\nintegration are complete. The FD family is Active for that operative work.\nFDV qualification is Active but partial; FDV-003 benefit remains Deferred and\nunqualified. The [handoff](../.ai-workspace/qualification/t008/handoff-001/README.md)\nretains exact evidence and gaps, including failed/partial ordinary actor trials.\nCurrent frozen dogfood models still represent selected methodology corpora.\n\nQualification separates deterministic checked properties, actual acquisition\nand executor effects, ordinary actor usability, independent semantic assessment\nand owner disposition under the selected method. Benefit requires matched\naccepted-result quality/cost evidence, including acquisition, F_P authoring,\nrefresh, invocation, retries, repair and review; graph use or fewer calls alone\nestablishes no improvement. Further qualification, owner acceptance and\nrelease remain open.\n\n## Independence\n\nGraphify is a build tenant of this common WHAT. It is not a separately composed\nAxiom Indexer Product. The Product Definition's composition is empty. This\nproject neither changes nor waits for v3, and has no membership in the existing\nSTDO release-matched cohort. Any later consumer adoption is separately selected.\nUpstream software used by a tenant is part of that tenant's HOW.\n\n## Product disposition authority\n\n\n################ SOURCE tool specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md {'lines': [89, 240]} sel_sha cbed803ae275c054debff15e65a49ab4a678e84734c71d67221b5943352a40f7 acq {}\n### REQ-AC-FD-005 — Assemble and check selected actor context\n\n**Input:** caller-selected frame/configuration and exact method packet contract,\nsubject/basis, seeds and governing dependency semantics, allowed acquisition\nroutes, supplied role/authority and actor envelope. **Output/checks:** an exact\nprojection of the supplied binding with actual acquired record/source content,\nsource references, declared closure and boundaries; a manifest of what was\nsupplied versus still to be acquired; and scoped completeness/identity/fit\nchecks under the selected contract. Where context capacity is declared, measure\nits stated boundary/unit before read, retaining any unmeasured/unknown host\ncontext. Preserve the selected method's qualifications, result relation and\nstop/refusal semantics. **Limit:** do not invent packet fields as a second method,\nsilently truncate required content or claim semantic sufficiency from closure,\nsize or schema. Exact late acquisition is visible and follows the supplied\nmethod contract. Owners: [RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) §11, RF-013/014;\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §2;\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §19 only when that profile is selected.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-006 — Preflight a Product-bound execution contract\n\n**Input:** caller-supplied work contract, governing outcome/grant, exact admission\nbinding/checks and any existing admission or permitted override evidence,\noperation/tools/territory/envelope and named durable result/evidence surface.\n**Output/checks:** deterministic preflight findings over those inputs and\nadmission evidence obtained from the selected Product-bound mechanism where\ninvoked, bound to exact contract identity and decision authority. Report missing\nor mismatched required support before dispatch; retain draft and admitted\ncoordinates separately under the method's own contract. **Limit:** a successful\nshape/context check, role name, ticket state or tool invocation cannot mint\nadmission or work authority. The tool neither drafts a new grant nor admits the\nupstream outcome. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §1 Admission;\n[TICK](fd-source-owner-map.md#tick) §5.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-007 — Dispatch, notify and observe under a supplied grant\n\n**Input:** exact preflighted activation/admission, selected executor operation,\nexisting grant, permitted tools/territory, material preconditions, effective\ncontext/settings and selected attempt/resource/observation conditions.\n**Output/checks:** invocation identity, actual supplied payload/settings,\nacknowledgments, output/partial-output and effect/termination observations with\nscope/time, retained attempts and decision-relevant return/exception/basis-change\nnotifications. Check material bindings before the named effect and expose\nchanged preconditions without silent rebase. **Limit:** the deterministic\nwrapper does not make F_P output deterministic or semantic evidence of success.\nRequests, delivery, evaluation, intended effects and their observed end remain\nseparate under the selected method; timeout/cancel/interruption preserve its\nunknown-effect semantics. Fallback observation is bounded by supplied conditions,\nnot a mandatory polling controller. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act)\n§1/3 Effects/5; [EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §6 if selected.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-008 — Capture and check a closed return\n\n**Input:** returned payload/transport evidence, original activation and return\ncontract, expected consumer, exact subject/basis and supplied currentness,\ndependency and independence predicates/evidence. **Output/checks:** preserved raw\nreturn and provenance, deterministic binding/format/currentness findings and\nthe exact declared evaluations, predicates, domain outcomes and residuals that\nwere actually returned. Identify stale/wrong-subject/wrong-basis, missing,\nduplicate and conflicting evidence without dropping it; expose non-consumable\nsupport/gaps to the declared consumer. **Limit:** do not relabel a historical\nverdict as a new verdict, manufacture a result for an unperformed evaluation or\ntreat schema validity as semantic assessment/acceptance. A transport failure is\nreported separately using the selected method contract. Owners:\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-012;\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §3/7;\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §4.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-009 — Prepare independently acquirable review evidence\n\n**Input:** exact review claim/candidate and composition boundary, caller-selected\nsource, comparison subjects, proof/evidence population and method-owned\nindependence/exposure contract. **Output/checks:** independently resolvable raw\nauthority/candidate/proof acquisition routes, acquired content where requested,\nexact byte/record comparisons, and separate assertion/expected-result versus\nexecution provenance. Support expectation recording before candidate exposure\nand preserve the actual acquisition/exposure record under the supplied contract.\nWorkers can acquire their implementation/proof context; Reviewers can inspect\nthe actual candidate, tests/fixtures and source without author-only privileges.\n**Limit:** diffs and trace/binding checks are not semantic findings, an independent\nverdict or adoption of a review recommendation as disposition. Owners:\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1–4/6;\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/10/13–16;\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §9/10/17/19 if selected.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-010 — Execute declared checks and method-owned joins\n\n**Input:** exact subject/observations, selected executable or reproducible\ndecidable predicate/proof contract and its provenance/domain/limits, or a\nselected method-owned conjunction/translation with required coverage and inputs.\n**Output/checks:** reproducible `F_D[v]` judgments for the properties actually\nevaluated, counterexamples/gaps, and joins computed only under the supplied\nqualified operator. Preserve source predicate, original domain outcomes,\nnot-performed assessments, uncovered obligations and incompatibilities as the\nowner contract requires. Retain assertion/observation and execution identities.\n**Limit:** do not invent an algebra or stronger claim, turn a necessary-condition\npass into full satisfaction, execute an unsupported arbitrary calculus operation\nor replace F_P/owner judgment. Owners: [AC](fd-source-owner-map.md#ac) §5;\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results/Assertions\nand observation; [EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1/2;\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §10.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-011 — Project and record existing work/evidence facts\n\n**Input:** selected authoritative work/evidence carriers, caller-selected view,\nor an already-authorized actor/owner record and exact named Writer interface,\ngrant, target preimage and update conditions. **Output/checks:** source-linked\nprojections of existing work, progress/support, residuals and next-action\nscope/support/owner; for an authorized write, the exact applied record and\nobserved effect/result identity or refusal. Preserve original owner wording\nseparately from interpretation and method-owned distinctions among verdict,\nrecommendation, disposition, checkpoint, closure and release. **Limit:** create\nno rival task ledger, owner decision, role transition or continuation grant;\nthe tool records a supplied decision, never mechanically adopts a review\nrecommendation or mutates as an F_P Executive/Reviewer. Owners:\n[PDEF](fd-source-owner-map.md#pdef) §8;\n[TICK](fd-source-owner-map.md#tick) §7;\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §5;\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §4;\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §6 if selected.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-012 — Compute affected refresh and prepare reusable handoff\n\n**Input:** old/current source observations, exact dependency/impact declarations,\ndeclared invalidators, existing results/rulings and caller-selected recovery or\nreuse contract. **Output/checks:** source/derived differences, affected projection\nand evidence candidates, missing dependency coverage, method-prescribed\ninvalidation/applicability check results where decidable, and a reconstructable\nhandoff of still-applicable support, original records/successors, residuals and\nunreconciled effects. Reacquire named current inputs for the next dependent\naction; retain partial writes rather than assuming a reset. **Limit:** do not\nerase history/frozen studies, rewrite old judgments onto new subjects, infer\nunaffectedness from absent edges, or require replay/rebuild of valid unchanged\nsupport merely because a session/role changed. F_P resolves unsupported semantic\nimpact or preservation premises. Owners: [FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found)\nChange impact and evidence reuse; [RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) §10;\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §5/7;\n[TICK](fd-source-owner-map.md#tick) §7.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-013 — Retain attempt, usage and uncertainty evidence\n\n**Input:** invocation/acquisition/check/refresh/repair/review attempt observations\nand selected accounting/resource contract. **Output/checks:** bound attempt and\ncost records with units, measured scope, elapsed versus summed actor intervals,\navailable usage/cache counters, partial/failed calls, unknown counters and any\ndeclared limit-check result. Aggregation is reproducible without double counting;\nanticipated costs remain separate from observations. **Limit:** unavailable\nbackend usage stays unknown, selected limits are not universal quotas, and\nfewer calls or faster deterministic checks do not prove lower accepted-result\ncost or improved F_P quality. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §6;\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1;\n[SPEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#spec) §8.\n\n","numLines":1013,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1013}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019MZGePGiWVcHkXq1fo8NFf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNAyaVv1vQnqsbFLCh1B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BavSSBH8SQj86wSaHB5vKY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -I -c '\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\nv=d[\"result\"][\"value\"]\nenv=v[\"envelope\"]\nprint(\"envelope keys:\",list(env.keys()))\np=env[\"payload\"]\nprint(\"payload keys:\",list(p.keys()))\nprint(\"acquisitions:\",json.dumps(p[\"acquisitions\"],indent=0))\nfor k in p:\n    if k not in (\"acquisitions\",\"result\",\"response\",\"request\"):\n        print(\"--\",k,\":\",json.dumps(p[k])[:1200])\nfor k in env:\n    if k!=\"payload\": print(\"== env\",k,\":\",json.dumps(env[k])[:1200])\nr=p.get(\"result\") or p.get(\"response\")\nif r:\n    print(\"result keys:\",list(r.keys()) if isinstance(r,dict) else type(r))\n    if isinstance(r,dict):\n        for k in r:\n            if k not in (\"acquired\",): print(\"   r.\",k,\":\",json.dumps(r[k])[:600])\n' /Users/jim/.claude/projects/-Users-jim-src-apps-specification-methodology-skills/628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38/tool-results/blpltfnmx.txt","description":"Extract acquisition ArtifactRefs and payload metadata from the evidence read"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3732,"cache_read_input_tokens":84431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3732},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38","uuid":"ecc46df7-0376-4180-971d-ed0fe8ade151","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:33:25.178Z","request_id":"req_011CgNAyaEHstQJeML1YbiC5